From 66302f45d2f21200069e09aff17f8a08dd24b25f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pat Wendorf <dungeons@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:18:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] displayid: check padding only over the bytes the section has
 left

_di_displayid_parse() walks the section's data blocks and then checks
that the bytes after the last one are zero. It passed that check the
size it computed for the cursor *before* the last data block, not after
it:

- A data block whose declared length runs past the section is reported
  and skipped, but parse_data_block() returns the declared length, so
  the cursor ends up beyond the section. With a length byte of 0xFF in
  a 126-byte section, is_all_zeroes() then reads from 135 to 256 bytes
  past the end of a 256-byte EDID (CVE-2026-112271).
- A data block that exactly fills the section leaves the cursor at the
  section's end, and the stale size made the check read past it: a
  false "Padding: Contains non-zero bytes" failure.

Recompute the remaining size from the final cursor, and skip the check
when nothing remains.

Reproduced with AddressSanitizer: an EDID copied into a heap buffer of
its own size and given to di_info_parse_edid() gives a
heap-buffer-overflow READ in is_all_zeroes (displayid.c:42) called from
_di_displayid_parse (displayid.c:697). With this change: no report,
the over-long block is still reported, and the exactly-filled section
no longer reports padding. meson test: 64/64 before and after.

DisplayID v2 sections have no data block parsing in 0.3.0, so
CVE-2026-112272 (displayid2.c, 0.4.0) does not apply to this version.

Upstream: not yet offered (no upstream fix as of 2026-10-23)
CVE: CVE-2026-112271

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 displayid.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/displayid.c b/displayid.c
index 2ea63be..072207a 100644
--- a/displayid.c
+++ b/displayid.c
@@ -694,7 +694,18 @@ _di_displayid_parse(struct di_displayid *displayid, const uint8_t *data,
 		assert(data_block_size > 0);
 		i += (size_t) data_block_size;
 	}
-	if (!is_all_zeroes(&data[i], max_data_block_size)) {
+	/* max_data_block_size still describes the cursor before the last data
+	 * block. A block whose declared length ran past the section (skipped
+	 * above with a failure) left i beyond the section's end, and one that
+	 * exactly filled it left i at the end: in both cases nothing remains to
+	 * check, and the old size made is_all_zeroes() read past the section,
+	 * and past the EDID buffer for a long enough block (CVE-2026-112271). */
+	if (i < section_size - 1)
+		max_data_block_size = section_size - 1 - i;
+	else
+		max_data_block_size = 0;
+	if (max_data_block_size > 0 &&
+	    !is_all_zeroes(&data[i], max_data_block_size)) {
 		if (max_data_block_size < DISPLAYID_DATA_BLOCK_HEADER_SIZE)
 			add_failure(displayid,
 				    "Not enough bytes remain (%zu) for a DisplayID data block and the DisplayID filler is non-0.",
